<Layout title="About ATECT Architecture | Maryland Architecture Firm" description="Learn about ATECT Architecture, founded in 2004, and its residential and commercial design approach serving Maryland, Washington, DC, and Virginia.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">About ATECT</div><h1>The Design Solution.</h1><p>ATECT Architecture is a residential and commercial design firm serving Maryland, Washington, DC and Virginia, with a focus on balancing comfort, practicality and beauty.</p></section>
<section class="split-about"><div><div class="about-image" style="background-image:url('https://atectarchitecture.com/assets/images/image05.jpg?v=5bc6d0ed')" role="img" aria-label="ATECT Architecture project photo"></div></div><div class="prose"><div class="eyebrow">Charlie Jones · Project Architect</div><h2>Experience grounded in practical design.</h2><p>Charlie Jones has worked as a Project Architect and Manager at ATECT Architecture since 2004, balancing practical functionality with design quality throughout the project process.</p><p>ATECT Architecture was founded in 2004. The firm's stated approach is to create inspiring projects that balance comfort, practicality and beauty while improving the quality of life for the people who use the spaces.</p><p>ATECT's work is primarily based in Maryland and the DC area, with a willingness to travel for exceptional projects.</p></div></div>
<section class="section alt"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Who we serve</div><h2>Design support for different project needs.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">ATECT's original service structure addresses homeowners, builders and design professionals.</p></div><div class="about-grid"><article><h3>Homeowners</h3><p>Residential design for additions, kitchen renovations, bathroom renovations, decks, porches and new homes, through the construction-document phase with project coordination and management.</p></article><article><h3>Builders</h3><p>Construction documents from design through the construction-document phase for residential, commercial, interior fit-outs and as-built projects.</p></article><article><h3>Design Professionals</h3><p>Subcontracting support including field measuring, design support and construction-document assistance.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="prose"><h2>A practical design process.</h2><p>Clear communication is central to the work. Early decisions establish direction; design development refines the solution; documentation communicates the final intent. Clients should understand what is being designed and why before moving into construction.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Service Area</strong><br />Maryland • Washington, DC • Virginia</div><a class="button dark" href="/contact">Discuss Your Project</a></section>
</Layout>
